1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,680
Stand up tall, reach out your hand.

2
00:00:03,840 --> 00:00:06,880
Cut through the wind and make a stand.

3
00:00:07,080 --> 00:00:11,240
The paint within brings
out a map of your own.

4
00:00:16,120 --> 00:00:19,680
To the left and the right,
all we saw stormy nights.

5
00:00:19,840 --> 00:00:22,960
All the rough winds and
waves coming day after day.

6
00:00:23,160 --> 00:00:26,180
And the values we had
were about to collapse.

7
00:00:26,360 --> 00:00:28,757
Oh, just where do we go next?

8
00:00:28,840 --> 00:00:35,420
And as we look down to the compass in
hand Is it showing us the right direction?

9
00:00:35,740 --> 00:00:38,617
All we know is nobody
here knows it for certain.

10
00:00:38,700 --> 00:00:41,937
So close your eyes and breathe in deeply.

11
00:00:42,020 --> 00:00:45,137
And listen to your soul.

12
00:00:45,220 --> 00:00:48,117
You'll see a path in front of you.

13
00:00:48,200 --> 00:00:51,537
And you'll know just where you need to go.

14
00:00:51,620 --> 00:00:55,817
So stand up tall, reach out your hand.

15
00:00:55,900 --> 00:00:59,037
Cut through the wind and make us stand.

16
00:00:59,120 --> 00:01:02,900
Don't let the darkness
win, just break through.

17
00:01:04,620 --> 00:01:08,137
I'll do it my own way,
that's what's best for me.

18
00:01:08,220 --> 00:01:11,777
And you do it your way,
that's how it's got to be.

19
00:01:11,860 --> 00:01:15,397
We're moving forward, now I'm ready.

20
00:01:15,480 --> 00:01:19,217
But at times it's okay
to get help on the way.

21
00:01:19,300 --> 00:01:21,757
For the future ahead, burning bright.

22
00:01:21,840 --> 00:01:24,237
For what's ahead you see.

23
00:01:24,320 --> 00:01:27,640
Is beyond your wildest dreams.

24
00:01:28,600 --> 00:01:31,757
So stand up tall, reach out your hand.

25
00:01:31,840 --> 00:01:34,977
Cut through the wind and make a stand.

26
00:01:35,060 --> 00:01:38,820
Don't let the darkness
win, just break through.

27
00:01:40,440 --> 00:01:44,077
We'll do it our way,
the best that we know.

28
00:01:44,160 --> 00:01:47,937
With tears and doubts and tone,
we'll go where we all wanna go.

29
00:01:48,020 --> 00:01:52,320
The page within brings colors of our own.

30
00:02:04,360 --> 00:02:06,480
I can grab Kaido's clouds?

31
00:02:06,840 --> 00:02:08,060
Of course I can!

32
00:02:08,360 --> 00:02:10,125
We're both dragons, after all!

33
00:02:19,560 --> 00:02:21,480
Even if I can't push it back,

34
00:02:22,020 --> 00:02:23,844
Perhaps I can stop its advance.

35
00:02:27,140 --> 00:02:30,660
Or even better, I can
change its direction.

36
00:02:32,160 --> 00:02:33,700
This is my duty.

37
00:02:34,260 --> 00:02:35,580
No one else can do it.

38
00:02:35,820 --> 00:02:36,740
I must.

39
00:02:37,600 --> 00:02:40,940
The capital will not be
destroyed under my watch.

40
00:02:41,900 --> 00:02:46,840
As its rightful Shogun, I will guide
the land of Wano to a new dawn.

41
00:02:56,960 --> 00:02:59,460
He shot beams from his eyes.

42
00:02:59,920 --> 00:03:01,140
Don't tell me.

43
00:03:19,180 --> 00:03:20,480
Is everyone alright?

44
00:03:21,080 --> 00:03:23,117
I think we need to find a new spot.

45
00:03:23,200 --> 00:03:24,847
Let us retreat further back.

46
00:03:27,580 --> 00:03:29,380
Chi-chi's gone! What?

47
00:03:29,720 --> 00:03:31,602
Did I lose him in the explosion?

48
00:03:31,860 --> 00:03:33,357
There's no time to search.

49
00:03:33,440 --> 00:03:35,616
We don't know when another might hit.

50
00:03:36,260 --> 00:03:37,140
Maybe so.

51
00:03:42,420 --> 00:03:43,620
I might die.

52
00:03:43,980 --> 00:03:45,677
But I don't want to leave him here.

53
00:03:45,760 --> 00:03:47,080
I'm sorry!

54
00:03:47,600 --> 00:03:48,880
Awesome, I know!

55
00:03:50,200 --> 00:03:52,300
Bet you know this one too!

56
00:03:54,360 --> 00:03:55,580
Henry Queen!

57
00:04:19,440 --> 00:04:21,220
Was that Niji's move?

58
00:04:23,280 --> 00:04:25,020
You're catching onvin smoke.

59
00:04:25,280 --> 00:04:26,677
Well, aren't you clever?

60
00:04:26,760 --> 00:04:27,680
Ha ha, idiot.

61
00:04:32,360 --> 00:04:33,948
Queen don't give it to you.

62
00:04:40,040 --> 00:04:42,360
So, did I ace the test or what?

63
00:04:42,520 --> 00:04:45,677
As you can tell, I did thorough
research on all of Jamba's.

64
00:04:45,760 --> 00:04:50,289
I can replicate any move that your
brothers do, except not make it look good!

65
00:04:52,840 --> 00:04:53,800
I don't care!

66
00:04:53,960 --> 00:04:55,557
I cut ties with those jerks!

67
00:04:55,640 --> 00:04:58,477
The idea was to show it to
you after you transformed,

68
00:04:58,560 --> 00:05:00,795
but you really screwed that up for me!

69
00:05:03,580 --> 00:05:05,237
Kicking your ass is one thing,

70
00:05:05,320 --> 00:05:08,857
but I can't really stick it to
Judge unless I beat you in the suit!

71
00:05:08,940 --> 00:05:12,175
That'd prove my superiority
beyond a shadow of a doubt!

72
00:05:12,820 --> 00:05:15,700
I don't give a crap about
your dumb rivalries!

73
00:05:16,620 --> 00:05:20,020
You know, I'm starting to
think that you don't like me!

74
00:05:23,920 --> 00:05:24,750
We're Queen!

75
00:05:37,980 --> 00:05:40,057
I think I nailed it right!

76
00:05:40,140 --> 00:05:43,728
You've probably been on the
receiving end of that one before!

77
00:05:55,280 --> 00:05:57,280
My beautiful arm!

78
00:06:00,480 --> 00:06:03,460
All right, punk, it's on now!

79
00:06:04,780 --> 00:06:06,540
What did I tell you?

80
00:06:07,560 --> 00:06:11,100
Keep talking about those bastards
and this is what you get?

81
00:06:11,920 --> 00:06:15,861
You telling me I gotta watch what
I say cause you're too sensitive!

82
00:06:17,640 --> 00:06:19,997
Let me make one thing clear.

83
00:06:20,080 --> 00:06:22,337
Suit or no suit you're going down!

84
00:06:22,420 --> 00:06:24,800
I've got everything I need right here.

85
00:06:27,220 --> 00:06:28,640
Let's end this.

86
00:06:33,360 --> 00:06:34,380
Let's save.

87
00:06:37,300 --> 00:06:38,130
Strike!

88
00:06:38,213 --> 00:06:39,043
Strike!

89
00:06:51,140 --> 00:06:53,787
What makes you think
you have the upper hand?

90
00:06:54,520 --> 00:06:55,500
Did you forget?

91
00:06:55,640 --> 00:06:59,052
I sent your ass flying once
already and I can do it again.

92
00:06:59,560 --> 00:07:02,266
It wasn't enough to win,
but I know that hurt.

93
00:07:02,940 --> 00:07:05,180
We've been fighting for a long time.

94
00:07:05,460 --> 00:07:06,557
You must be wearing down.

95
00:07:06,640 --> 00:07:07,470
I'm ready.

96
00:07:07,580 --> 00:07:11,620
Like it or not, I've
already accepted my fate.

97
00:07:14,000 --> 00:07:16,440
I'm not the same guy you fought before.

98
00:07:21,200 --> 00:07:22,400
Inferious Weakley!

99
00:07:22,940 --> 00:07:25,480
You ain't never had a foe like me.

100
00:07:29,900 --> 00:07:32,640
If you're not going to use it, I will.

101
00:07:33,200 --> 00:07:34,060
Stealth blast!

102
00:07:35,200 --> 00:07:37,660
You really can do it all, can't you?

103
00:07:40,240 --> 00:07:41,400
Got you now.

104
00:07:41,820 --> 00:07:45,980
Your back is wide open, smoke sloppily.

105
00:07:47,780 --> 00:07:48,610
What?

106
00:07:48,760 --> 00:07:50,525
How the hell did he disappear?

107
00:07:53,000 --> 00:07:55,118
But he doesn't have to suit anymore.

108
00:07:55,540 --> 00:07:58,480
He must be moving so fast
he's become invisible.

109
00:08:02,100 --> 00:08:04,277
You'll run out of stamina soon enough.

110
00:08:04,360 --> 00:08:06,420
Then he'll have to show himself.

111
00:08:08,940 --> 00:08:11,234
Didn't think this one through, did you?

112
00:08:16,600 --> 00:08:18,480
Get the hell out of here, rat.

113
00:08:19,580 --> 00:08:20,410
Shoujou!

114
00:08:21,020 --> 00:08:22,680
Thank goodness you're okay.

115
00:08:23,360 --> 00:08:24,190
Let's go.

116
00:08:25,480 --> 00:08:28,837
We have to hurry to a safe spot
before those two start fighting again.

117
00:08:28,920 --> 00:08:29,880
Awesome-y!

118
00:08:30,300 --> 00:08:32,080
That trap is still alive!

119
00:08:32,420 --> 00:08:33,260
Damn it!

120
00:08:43,940 --> 00:08:47,220
Now where did you run off to, Thinsmoke?

121
00:08:51,460 --> 00:08:52,757
Could you help me?

122
00:08:52,840 --> 00:08:54,240
Whoever you are!

123
00:08:54,880 --> 00:08:57,017
Please, I have nothing to do with this!

124
00:08:57,100 --> 00:08:58,877
I'm just a geisha from the capital!

125
00:08:58,960 --> 00:08:59,790
Awesome man!

126
00:08:59,960 --> 00:09:01,666
You're supposed to be in bed!

127
00:09:01,860 --> 00:09:05,960
I came by asking for your services,
and they said you had a headache!

128
00:09:06,280 --> 00:09:09,927
Well, you look nice and healthy
to me, you filthy little liar!

129
00:09:10,680 --> 00:09:15,120
I try to be a good customer to
you, and this is what I get?

130
00:09:15,620 --> 00:09:17,032
Rejection and deception?

131
00:09:17,440 --> 00:09:20,020
You're getting too
cocky for your own good!

132
00:09:22,840 --> 00:09:28,020
You were supposed to be my number
one girl now that Komurasaki is gone.

133
00:09:28,620 --> 00:09:30,420
I won't forgive you.

134
00:09:30,660 --> 00:09:34,780
You'll pay for lying to me and for
all those times you turned me down.

135
00:09:35,160 --> 00:09:37,080
This is divine punishment.

136
00:09:38,060 --> 00:09:39,860
I want to go home.

137
00:09:48,320 --> 00:09:52,197
Your behavior required
swift and punitive action.

138
00:09:52,280 --> 00:09:57,040
It's only natural justice has been served

139
00:10:04,760 --> 00:10:10,820
You're not showing an ounce of remorse looks
like I need to punish you a second time

140
00:10:18,660 --> 00:10:22,617
think about what you've
gained an exoskeleton muscle

141
00:10:22,700 --> 00:10:26,657
strength and mobility more
tools in my arsenal that's

142
00:10:26,740 --> 00:10:32,957
all if i fine-tune my
armament Haki and cover my

143
00:10:33,040 --> 00:10:36,417
exoskeleton with it my legs
will become stronger than ever.

144
00:10:36,500 --> 00:10:40,265
They'll be capable of supporting
even hotter flames than before.

145
00:10:40,560 --> 00:10:42,160
This is Fire Chamba.

146
00:10:43,100 --> 00:10:45,360
Faster acceleration, heavier weight.

147
00:10:45,580 --> 00:10:47,227
I don't have any more doubt.

148
00:10:47,360 --> 00:10:50,360
Don't you know that a man
should never hit a woman?

149
00:10:50,860 --> 00:10:53,660
That's been a fact since
the age of dinosaurs.

150
00:10:54,420 --> 00:10:56,860
I should have known, scumbag.

151
00:10:57,120 --> 00:10:58,540
Of course it was you.

152
00:10:59,260 --> 00:11:00,320
Call Yang Kong.

153
00:11:09,300 --> 00:11:12,360
Where did Master Tweet
come from? Don't worry.

154
00:11:12,720 --> 00:11:14,620
Just leave him to me. Okay.

155
00:11:18,720 --> 00:11:20,720
There you are, Venge Smoke!

156
00:11:20,980 --> 00:11:22,040
Now die!

157
00:11:31,100 --> 00:11:32,040
That's cool!

158
00:11:33,900 --> 00:11:34,730
Alarun!

159
00:11:36,980 --> 00:11:38,320
Shumar Miftas!

160
00:11:39,280 --> 00:11:40,700
Tendron! Blanche!

161
00:11:41,340 --> 00:11:43,260
K! Warre! Jares!

162
00:11:44,380 --> 00:11:45,210
No!

163
00:11:58,880 --> 00:12:01,937
Now that has been smoke
power five ever three years!

164
00:12:02,020 --> 00:12:05,700
But you're still trying to
deny the truth, Jeremiah boy?

165
00:12:05,920 --> 00:12:07,317
You're the one in denial.

166
00:12:07,400 --> 00:12:08,720
I'm my own man.

167
00:12:09,400 --> 00:12:11,812
Repeating that crap doesn't make it true.

168
00:12:15,220 --> 00:12:17,600
This dish still needs its final touch.

169
00:12:18,100 --> 00:12:21,137
Dinosaur meat's tough, but
there's nothing I can't cook.

170
00:12:21,220 --> 00:12:22,760
Let's finish this already.

171
00:12:23,180 --> 00:12:24,220
Oh, shut up!

172
00:12:24,440 --> 00:12:26,757
You're a failed cyborg and a failed human!

173
00:12:26,840 --> 00:12:29,546
I won't lose to a
second-rate science project!

174
00:12:55,380 --> 00:12:59,060
Now get lost, you asshole!

175
00:13:02,020 --> 00:13:02,850
No!

176
00:13:32,020 --> 00:13:32,850
Don't worry.

177
00:13:33,280 --> 00:13:35,740
Your little friend is safe. Jaggy!

178
00:13:36,160 --> 00:13:37,480
I'm so relieved.

179
00:13:37,920 --> 00:13:39,567
Make sure you keep him safe.

180
00:13:39,660 --> 00:13:40,601
I'll do my best.

181
00:13:40,740 --> 00:13:41,799
Thank you so much.

182
00:13:48,780 --> 00:13:51,427
Sanji was making some
of that rat food again.

183
00:13:55,340 --> 00:13:57,820
And you take good care of her too, okay?

184
00:14:00,520 --> 00:14:01,500
Your wound?

185
00:14:02,580 --> 00:14:06,160
You're not still pleading, are you?

186
00:14:06,580 --> 00:14:07,580
You should be.

187
00:14:08,600 --> 00:14:09,840
Are you okay?

188
00:14:10,160 --> 00:14:11,140
We need help!

189
00:14:11,380 --> 00:14:13,204
Someone bring a first aid, kid!

190
00:14:16,440 --> 00:14:22,160
Just remember, our mother selflessly gave
her life to protect you and your humanity.

191
00:14:24,040 --> 00:14:28,560
That's why you're kinder
and more tender than anyone.

192
00:14:30,780 --> 00:14:35,177
The battle in the pleasure hall of
the skull dome has come to an end.

193
00:14:35,260 --> 00:14:39,400
The winner is Sanji.

194
00:14:49,520 --> 00:14:51,117
I thought so.

195
00:14:51,200 --> 00:14:53,957
Something happens when the
flames on his back go out.

196
00:14:54,040 --> 00:14:55,320
He speeds up.

197
00:14:57,460 --> 00:15:00,640
But his defense, on the
other hand, gets weaker.

198
00:15:03,540 --> 00:15:06,780
He destroyed Master King's mask. Oh, man.

199
00:15:07,020 --> 00:15:09,397
And it looks like the
rumors about him are true.

200
00:15:09,480 --> 00:15:12,680
Black wings, white hair, brown skin.

201
00:15:14,820 --> 00:15:19,291
If we tipped off the government, we'd
get a hundred million bear rebounding.

202
00:15:20,480 --> 00:15:23,540
Hypothetically, that is
Imperial Flaming Wings.

203
00:15:30,000 --> 00:15:31,706
The castle's already burning.

204
00:15:31,860 --> 00:15:32,742
Give it a rest.

205
00:15:33,340 --> 00:15:37,987
You gotta keep your cool and set an
example for your men, not set them on fire.

206
00:15:40,040 --> 00:15:41,600
Why not step outside?

207
00:15:41,920 --> 00:15:43,332
You seem a little tense.

208
00:15:43,500 --> 00:15:46,437
That hundred million berry
thing really got to you, huh?

209
00:15:46,520 --> 00:15:48,108
Hell of a bounty for intel.

210
00:15:48,740 --> 00:15:50,360
What tribe are you from?

211
00:15:57,000 --> 00:15:59,529
Why bother asking when
you're about to die?

212
00:16:27,180 --> 00:16:29,580
Whatever his tribe is, it must be rare.

213
00:16:30,100 --> 00:16:31,512
But that doesn't matter.

214
00:16:31,760 --> 00:16:33,701
I have to find a way to beat him.

215
00:16:35,280 --> 00:16:36,110
Dammit.

216
00:16:36,193 --> 00:16:37,572
I'm running out of time.

217
00:16:38,000 --> 00:16:39,657
But this goes on much longer.

218
00:16:39,740 --> 00:16:41,858
A sword will kill me before he does.

219
00:16:45,800 --> 00:16:48,329
You are far more
dangerous than I expected.

220
00:16:51,180 --> 00:16:52,377
Yeah, same.

221
00:16:52,460 --> 00:16:57,720
Your reign has gone on for long
enough, as tyrants end as pirates.

222
00:16:58,100 --> 00:16:59,120
Step aside.

223
00:16:59,740 --> 00:17:01,140
Rather arrogant, Arsha.

224
00:17:01,360 --> 00:17:02,940
This is Kaido's destiny.

225
00:17:03,220 --> 00:17:05,514
He will become the king of the pirates!

226
00:17:06,020 --> 00:17:09,860
I'm sorry, but that dream ends here.

227
00:17:13,300 --> 00:17:14,800
King of Hell!

228
00:17:17,320 --> 00:17:19,060
Three-sword style!

229
00:17:25,680 --> 00:17:26,510
Pugatory!

230
00:17:30,440 --> 00:17:31,840
Onigiri!

231
00:17:52,460 --> 00:17:53,820
You gave me this life.

232
00:17:54,060 --> 00:17:55,200
I owe it to you.

233
00:17:57,660 --> 00:17:58,490
Interesting.

234
00:17:58,573 --> 00:18:01,044
I see why the world
government won't let you go.

235
00:18:01,420 --> 00:18:03,240
You're a Lunarian, huh?

236
00:18:04,480 --> 00:18:07,280
I saw your durability
test earlier. Impressive.

237
00:18:12,980 --> 00:18:17,451
I'm getting out of this dump, and then
I'm going to start a new pirate crew.

238
00:18:18,920 --> 00:18:21,660
What do you want to do, guinea pig?

239
00:18:30,520 --> 00:18:37,500
I'm gonna turn this boring world upside
down if you want to come that's your choice

240
00:18:40,280 --> 00:18:41,940
You think you can do it?

241
00:18:44,200 --> 00:18:45,320
Change the world?

242
00:18:47,380 --> 00:18:49,880
I'm the only one who can do it.

243
00:18:57,480 --> 00:19:00,017
The test subjects are
escaping the facility.

244
00:19:00,100 --> 00:19:02,817
Stop them at any cost! Roger that.

245
00:19:02,900 --> 00:19:04,460
Taking this shot.

246
00:19:07,500 --> 00:19:09,237
They aren't chasing us.

247
00:19:09,320 --> 00:19:12,177
No, they sure aren't.

248
00:19:12,260 --> 00:19:13,580
Open fire!

249
00:19:19,200 --> 00:19:20,553
The bullets don't work.

250
00:19:20,840 --> 00:19:21,780
What do we do?

251
00:19:25,380 --> 00:19:27,120
No, no, no, no, no.

252
00:19:27,440 --> 00:19:29,160
What the hell was that?

253
00:19:31,440 --> 00:19:32,270
Nothing.

254
00:19:39,680 --> 00:19:40,680
Oh, yeah.

255
00:19:40,900 --> 00:19:42,217
I almost forgot to ask.

256
00:19:42,300 --> 00:19:43,600
You got a name?

257
00:19:44,340 --> 00:19:45,200
It's Albear.

258
00:19:45,860 --> 00:19:48,140
Well, Albear, you're very strong.

259
00:19:49,560 --> 00:19:52,440
From here on out, I'll call you King.

260
00:19:54,500 --> 00:19:55,460
Fine with me.

261
00:19:56,180 --> 00:19:58,860
You watch my back, and I'll watch yours.

262
00:19:59,380 --> 00:20:01,040
I'll never sell you out.

263
00:20:01,580 --> 00:20:04,051
You're my right-hand man to the end, King.

264
00:20:17,180 --> 00:20:19,900
This world only has proof for one ruler!

265
00:20:20,460 --> 00:20:21,900
The flames are burning.

266
00:20:22,220 --> 00:20:23,440
I can't attack him.

267
00:20:25,080 --> 00:20:26,360
Die, Ramen!

268
00:20:27,420 --> 00:20:29,900
Imperial Flaming Wings!

269
00:20:42,940 --> 00:20:45,220
What the hell was that? Magma?

270
00:21:17,660 --> 00:21:19,340
It's a damned weapon!

271
00:21:23,180 --> 00:21:25,040
These swords are treasures!

272
00:21:25,440 --> 00:21:27,160
I'm not letting them go!

273
00:21:52,140 --> 00:21:54,240
He's sped up. This is it.

274
00:21:54,500 --> 00:21:55,580
I can cut him.

275
00:22:01,960 --> 00:22:02,790
Burnt it!

276
00:22:23,940 --> 00:22:26,020
See, you figured out my trick.

277
00:22:27,020 --> 00:22:28,960
That's very clever of you.

278
00:22:29,440 --> 00:22:30,880
You're damn right I did.

279
00:22:31,280 --> 00:22:34,260
Now nothing can stop me from beating you.

280
00:22:36,420 --> 00:22:37,820
Ahhhhhhh!

281
00:22:52,280 --> 00:22:53,680
Ultra!

282
00:22:55,000 --> 00:22:57,180
Take your trap!

283
00:23:13,960 --> 00:23:15,784
Why are you trying to block me?

284
00:23:15,900 --> 00:23:17,665
I thought you were invincible!

285
00:23:18,180 --> 00:23:21,340
Or are you scared what
might attack my duty?

286
00:23:24,800 --> 00:23:27,040
Oh, my God.

287
00:24:06,880 --> 00:24:10,600
You are biologically
incapable of defeating me!

288
00:24:12,500 --> 00:24:14,980
Blaming biologists is a weak excuse.

289
00:24:15,340 --> 00:24:16,957
I won't limit myself like that.

290
00:24:17,040 --> 00:24:22,420
I shall remember you for your brave
resorts, or your arrogance, I should say.

291
00:24:23,400 --> 00:24:25,700
I'll carve it into your memory myself!

292
00:24:26,000 --> 00:24:28,706
Do I seriously doubt
you'll live through this?

293
00:24:34,440 --> 00:24:36,520
Imperial Bellamy Frames!

294
00:25:06,220 --> 00:25:07,180
Oh, my God.

295
00:25:17,380 --> 00:25:20,720
King of Hell, Three-Sword Serpents!

296
00:25:24,660 --> 00:25:27,180
One hundred and three mercies!

297
00:25:31,040 --> 00:25:34,460
This is the end for you, Rorodawa!

298
00:25:39,600 --> 00:25:41,280
Dragon damnation!

299
00:26:14,300 --> 00:26:16,660
Ah, Kaido...

300
00:26:17,780 --> 00:26:18,610
I...

301
00:26:18,700 --> 00:26:21,112
You still holding on to that, Dream King?

302
00:26:22,040 --> 00:26:23,800
You really think I'm Joy Boy?

303
00:26:24,280 --> 00:26:25,937
I mean, I'm not complaining here.

304
00:26:26,020 --> 00:26:30,255
But are you sure the world I'm looking
to make is the one that you want?

305
00:26:31,520 --> 00:26:33,402
Well, a legend is just a legend.

306
00:26:33,840 --> 00:26:36,899
And I could never ask for
more than you've given me.

307
00:26:37,560 --> 00:26:39,031
I'm alive because of you.

308
00:26:39,860 --> 00:26:41,240
My life is yours.

309
00:26:41,980 --> 00:26:43,817
So you must remain undefeated.

310
00:26:43,900 --> 00:26:46,540
and I will do the same.

311
00:26:48,280 --> 00:26:51,020
You will be king of the pirates.

312
00:27:01,340 --> 00:27:07,060
I know that you need nothing less than
the greatest swordsman in the world.

313
00:27:17,800 --> 00:27:20,737
So until the day comes
when I defeat him and take

314
00:27:20,820 --> 00:27:25,597
his title I promise you
that I will never lose.

315
00:27:25,680 --> 00:27:30,860
Again is that okay King of the Pirates?

316
00:27:35,780 --> 00:27:37,237
I will become

317
00:27:37,320 --> 00:27:43,880
the king of hell.

318
00:27:58,740 --> 00:28:04,760
The Battle of the Ritebring Tower outside
the Skull Dome has come to an end.

319
00:28:11,760 --> 00:28:13,360
The winner, Zoro.

320
00:28:13,880 --> 00:28:15,420
Thank you.
